    "body": "fix on issue/2636-see-through-wireframe · PR #2931 · pinned by `see_through_wireframe_draws_each_edge_and_no_face`, `the_see_through_entry_exists_sets_its_mode_and_shows_the_check`, `the_see_through_mode_is_kept_in_the_view_file`, `in_see_through_a_click_over_a_hidden_edge_picks_that_edge`, `the_wireframe_switch_leaves_see_through_for_the_default_mode` · merges at the next cut\n\nPR #2931 is stacked on PR #2835. Merge #2835 first.\nPR #2835 gives \"Shaded\" without edges, the draw list of each mode and the saved display mode.\nPR #2931 adds \"Wireframe, see-through\" to the Display menu, the draw list and the feature pick.\nThe display choice is in the Display menu of the viewport toolbar (#2818), not in the Browser pane.\nHidden edges do not draw in a lighter tone. The decision record in the PR gives the reason.\n",
